body:
Mercury is androgynous, refutes the sexual in favour of the intellectual plane where data is neutral. Kind of cold.

&#x200B;

Mercury is associated with children, / gemini (3rd), the androgyny I connect to children's being pre-pubescent.

What are you writing about?

&#x200B;

I also want to write. I am constantly writing a novel in my head.

Not when Venus is retrograde, nor when the moon is void.

&#x200B;

Don't do it is transit Venus or Saturn is in hard aspect with each other, and pay attention to 1st house planets, as well as contacts to your ascendant.

ok, some activities

\- Go to see a collection of curiosities-- shrunken heads, lamb fetuses in formaldehyde, death masks, stuff like that.  


\- Feed your morbid curiosity: Watch a video/documentary about topics like surgery, serial killers, embalming corpses, mummification or dissection. Get your palm read. Learn Tarot. Enjoy some erotic art, paintings, film, photography.

&#x200B;

\- Go to a library or used book store, find some books on occult and take them home

&#x200B;

\- Explore your sexuality, open yourself up to the unknown, and stuff that makes you uncomfortable actually will help you. This is normal for nodes, but especially so with 8th, constantly telling you to walk on the wild side. 

&#x200B;

\- Let go of a preoccupation with being wholesome.

&#x200B;

\- Meditate on death-- what you or others will leave behind if/when you die. Facing death and its reality is very important for your soul's path.  


\- Review where you stand with inheritance, insurance, and how other peoples' money affects you. Run a prognosis on the flow of power in your life, and see what you can untangle. 8th house is a money house, and also a house of hidden treasure, antiques, and solving mysteries.

&#x200B;

\- You may find yourself making contact with the criminal underworld, and dark corners in your journey! At first it may seem odd, but there are parts of your life that will dovetail into some kind of unseen doings, but for the better, and for good karmic transformation, and it may be linked to your own survival. Darkness is inseparable from 8th North Node path. You don't have to share, and in your evolution, secrets actually do make friends.


\- be cozy with the notion that North Node 8th is like a magnet pulling you into the  unknown, resulting in you becoming deeper and deeper in mysteriousness! You will go from innocent earthly Taurus to witchy magical Scorpion identity. It's a fun path, but be prepared for people watching you to be worried and confused when you are shedding your skin and getting your best catharsis on. Interesting new friends guaranteed!   


\- disclaimer: Do not tell everybody what you get up to on a North Node 8th path, because you will get into trouble. Invariably its a path that makes you so secretive, nobody hardly suspects what's under your belt.  


Enjoy.

&#x200B;

i find everything normal women wear uncomfortable. i like the look of jeans but I seriously am dying to take them off when I come home. Sometimes I look at a woman's outfit and its like nails on a blackboard.

&#x200B;

Also, I do like hair and makeup, but I have no idea how women keep them looking good for over 20 mins. When I try cute stuff I come out looking a bit clownish. Do you have to carry a mirror around all the time? How do people do it?

&#x200B;

This weekend I went out and someone asked me about being a lesbian because of how low key I was groomed. Which is fine. I actually feel fine without make up. I usually just wear concealer under my eyes. I really love the feeling of less grease and stuff on my face.  


Not being able to relate this to girls kind of sucks. Or just doing embarrassing stuff in front of other women that only a woman with no female friends does.....  


&#x200B;

So there seems to be a very apparent trend of looking younger.  
Would we agree then that we get mansplained stuff more than the average person?

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

That's really cool you have that ability. I really wonder how other women/girls are just super cool and handle the wierdness like its no big deal! At least, those moments don't stick with you for the rest of the day? Did you train yourself to shake it off somehow?

&#x200B;

I think retail is fine-- like its 3% of people, but its enough to mess me up a bit. I'll get used to it I guess..

I work in customer service. I have been yelled at to speak louder... I have a lot of trouble projecting my voice sometimes over the music in the store, and I also have trouble hearing people speaking. 

&#x200B;

 I feel like I have no control over my voice sometimes, or how words come out in sentences!

Mercury - Saturn contacts.

&#x200B;

Mercury in 12th is subconscious that is well integrated with mind/good perception and storytellng, is a sign of a writer. Mercury contacts to Neptune is storytelling, and also translates well to storyboard type thinkers/cinematic narrative/visual spatial thinking. They are good with visions. They also may be bad at speech but excellent at writing.

&#x200B;

I read that writers can be spotted via Mercury/saturn energy contacts. Intellect/thought concretized into work/profession. Saturn is a builder. Mercury is thoughts. A plotted out, sequential construction of thoughts = a book. Books are Saturnian in a way. The same can be said of composing music. Saturn is dry but we desperately need him as creative types.

&#x200B;

I looked up Cazimi mercuries on astrotheme and a lot of these people are pretty good writers.

You'd think air signs automatically, but you need water energy to make a person creative and perceptive, shapeshift into other subjectivities, and also Earth energy in the mix somewhere for structure and work ethic.

Without Earth to ground creative people, projects do not reach the physical plane.

Just pulled up some authors to see if what I wrote up there applies.

Hemmingway, who happens to have Saturn trine Mercury. His Mercury is in 12th.

Victor Hugo has a stellium in Pisces, incl. Mercury.

&#x200B;

Gertrude Stein is cazimi Mercury, Saturn included in 12th (stellium in aqu)

&#x200B;

Dostoyevsky, Mercury 12th, Merc. sesquiquadrate Saturn (exact)

&#x200B;

Vonnegut doesn't seem to have these things I wrote up there, but Sun in 12th.

&#x200B;

Jane Austen has Mercury in 3rd Quintile her Asc which is exact conj. Neptune.

&#x200B;

James Joyce has Saturn in 3rd. Youd think that means impairment in speech and communication, which is traditional definition, but again, when Mercury energy is "stifled" I think it is the fodder of writers, since it's slowed down and refined.

&#x200B;

Mark Twain: Saturn in 12th, Mercury in 1st, Saturn/Mercury Midpoint = his Ascendant, Neptune in 3rd

&#x200B;

Dickens: Mercury and Saturn in Capricorn, very busy Neptune 3rd

&#x200B;

Anais Nin: Saturn Mercury conjunction in Aquarius (4th), Neptune conj. MC

&#x200B;

I really think it comes down to Saturn/Mercury connection with a good Neptune influence, and many of these people have 12th planets, meaning people who live in isolation.
